{"id": 5836, "name": "Nordland Park Campground", "read": "2026-10-15", "pages": [{"url": "https://cityofarlingtonsd.com/camping", "lines": [" | Government | Recreation | Camping | The City of Arlington | The City of Arlington maintains two campgrounds inside the city limits. Both are free for non-electrical spots but if electricity is needed the cost is just $10.00 per night. Most camper pads have a 50 amp hookup option. | Maxwell Park Campground | 101 North Main Street | This campground is convenient to all downtown activities. There are 4 camper pads lo", "ain Street | This campground is convenient to all downtown activities. There are 4 camper pads located in Maxwell Park (1-50 amp pad and 3-30 amp pads). There is also grass area for tent campers at no charge. There is a $10.00/night charge for the electricity and a camper dump station. | Nordland Park Campground | Campground is located on the north side of Lake Arlington on Highways 14 & 81. This campground offers a ", "scenic view of Lake Arlington and Nordland Isle. | Lake Arlington | There are 5 camper pads located at Lake Arlington (3-50 amp pads and 2-30 amp pads). There is also grass area for tent campers at no charge. There is a $10.00/night charge for the electricity. | Lake Poinsett | Located 14 miles northeast of Arlington is the Lake Poinsett Recreation Area State Park. Two campgrounds offer 112 sites with two comfort sta"]}]}
{"id": 5845, "name": "Spearfish City Campground", "read": "2026-10-15", "pages": [{"url": "https://www.spearfish.gov/185/Campground", "lines": ["rom Highway 14 is closed. Please enter the campground by going through town using the directions on the side of this page. | Off-Season Camping | The off-season runs from October 1 through April 30. We allow camping for $21 per night plus a $3 booking fee from October 1 to October 31 and January 1 to April 30 . The campground is closed for the months of November and December due to a holiday event. During the off-sea"]}, {"url": "https://www.spearfish.gov/Facilities/Facility/Details/Spearfish-City-Campground-1", "lines": ["ugh October (closed November and December for a holiday event) with full amenities available from May 1 through September 30, all dependent on the weather and staffing availability. Off season camping is available for a $20 fee. The dump station is available during the off season, but there is no rinse water. | Go to Calendar Availability | Subscribe to Calendar Updates ▲ Back to top Agendas & Minutes | Ordinances | "], "via": "Spearfish City Campground"}, {"url": "https://www.spearfish.gov/DocumentCenter/View/207/Campground-Map-PDF?bidId=", "pdf": true, "via": "Campground Map (PDF)"}, {"url": "https://www.spearfish.gov/gallery.aspx?AID=2", "lines": [], "via": "Campsite Photos"}, {"url": "https://www.spearfish.gov/187/Fees", "lines": ["ess and more. | Website Sign In | About Us | Parks | Facilities | Cemetery | Home | Departments | Parks, Recreation & Forestry | Facilities | Campground | Fees | 2027 Fees | Taxes are included in rates. A non-refundable $3 booking fee will be added to each reservation. | 2027 Regular Full Hookup Sites | Reservations open on June 1 the year before. The full hookup sites have water, sewer, and 50 and 30-amp electricity", "ndable $3 booking fee will be added to each reservation. | 2027 Regular Full Hookup Sites | Reservations open on June 1 the year before. The full hookup sites have water, sewer, and 50 and 30-amp electricity. The fee is $52 per night . | 2027 Premium Full Hookup Sites (P1-P6, 30 and 1) | Reservations open on June 1 the year before. These sites have water, sewer, 50 and 30-amp electricity, a larger firepit, hammock, a", " night . | 2027 Premium Full Hookup Sites (P1-P6, 30 and 1) | Reservations open on June 1 the year before. These sites have water, sewer, 50 and 30-amp electricity, a larger firepit, hammock, and a gas grill. The fee is $63 per night. | Tents are not allowed on any full hookup sites. | 2027 Primitive Sites | Reservations for primitive camping may be made ahead of time and are encouraged during busy holiday weekends. ", "ncouraged during busy holiday weekends. The physical location you are able to set up is on a first-come first-serve basis. Sites are not labeled or designated, and the camping is open, so sites are priced per unit (i.e. $26 per night per tent). | Site Use Fee | Tents, Pick-up Campers, Van Campers, and Motorcycle Campers | $26 per night per unit | | Motor Homes, Travel Trailers, 5th Wheels, and Pop-up Campers (all siz", "er unit (i.e. $26 per night per tent). | Site Use Fee | Tents, Pick-up Campers, Van Campers, and Motorcycle Campers | $26 per night per unit | | Motor Homes, Travel Trailers, 5th Wheels, and Pop-up Campers (all sizes) | $42 per night per unit | | | | | | | | | Rally Rates | Store Items | Off Season | Rally Rates | 2027 Rally rates are effective the Friday of the start of Rally through the final Sunday of Rally. Pleas", "ffective the Friday of the start of Rally through the final Sunday of Rally. Please call 605.642.1340 to make your reservation. | Site Type/Use Fee | Primitive Sites - Tent, Pickup Camper, Van Camper, and MC Trailer | | $42 per night | | Primitive Recreational Vehicle Sites - Motor homes, Travel Trailers, 5th Wheels, and Pop-up Campers (all sizes) | | $58 per night | | Full Hookup Sites | | $125 per night | | Premium", " Type/Use Fee | Primitive Sites - Tent, Pickup Camper, Van Camper, and MC Trailer | | $42 per night | | Primitive Recreational Vehicle Sites - Motor homes, Travel Trailers, 5th Wheels, and Pop-up Campers (all sizes) | | $58 per night | | Full Hookup Sites | | $125 per night | | Premium Hookup Sites (P1-P6, 30 & 1) | $136 per night | | Store Items | Item Fee | Firewood | $7 per bundle | | ICE - 7 lbs. Cubed | 16 lbs. ", "s, Travel Trailers, 5th Wheels, and Pop-up Campers (all sizes) | | $58 per night | | Full Hookup Sites | | $125 per night | | Premium Hookup Sites (P1-P6, 30 & 1) | $136 per night | | Store Items | Item Fee | Firewood | $7 per bundle | | ICE - 7 lbs. Cubed | 16 lbs. Cubed | $4 | $8 | | Non-Guest Shower Use | $6 per person | | Non-Resident Dump Station Use | | $5 | | Campground sticker | $3 | | 1 Seater Pedal Cart Ren", "ites (P1-P6, 30 & 1) | $136 per night | | Store Items | Item Fee | Firewood | $7 per bundle | | ICE - 7 lbs. Cubed | 16 lbs. Cubed | $4 | $8 | | Non-Guest Shower Use | $6 per person | | Non-Resident Dump Station Use | | $5 | | Campground sticker | $3 | | 1 Seater Pedal Cart Rental | $10/hour | | 2 Seater Pedal Cart Rental | $15/hour | | Baseball caps | $20 per cap | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | |", " | $8 | | Non-Guest Shower Use | $6 per person | | Non-Resident Dump Station Use | | $5 | | Campground sticker | $3 | | 1 Seater Pedal Cart Rental | $10/hour | | 2 Seater Pedal Cart Rental | $15/hour | | Baseball caps | $20 per cap | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | Off Season | Off-season camping is available from October 1 through October 30 and January 1 through April 30 . The cost to ", "ball caps | $20 per cap | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | Off Season | Off-season camping is available from October 1 through October 30 and January 1 through April 30 . The cost to camp is $21.00 per night plus a $3 booking fee per reservation. To camp, please make a reservation online to secure your spot. | There is no camping in November or December due to a holiday event. | Electrici"], "via": "Fees"}, {"url": "https://www.spearfish.gov/188/Reservations", "lines": []}, {"url": "https://www.spearfish.gov/190/Festival-in-the-Park-Reservations", "lines": [], "via": "Festival in the Park Reservations"}, {"url": "https://www.spearfish.gov/191/Sturgis-Rally-Reservations", "lines": [" at your site without the registered guest staying as well. | Please inform the campground office of any additional campers staying in your recreational vehicle ( RV ) at your site. | Rates and Payment: | 2027 sites are $125 per night for full hook-up (FHU). Premium FHU sites are $136 per night. Primitive RV rate is $58 per night. Tent rate is $42 per night. Guests wanting to park tow trailers next to their tents wil", "aying in your recreational vehicle ( RV ) at your site. | Rates and Payment: | 2027 sites are $125 per night for full hook-up (FHU). Premium FHU sites are $136 per night. Primitive RV rate is $58 per night. Tent rate is $42 per night. Guests wanting to park tow trailers next to their tents will be charged for another tent space. | The campground does not accept checks as a form of payment. Please pay with cash, money", "ts at Hookup Sites: | If you wish to have friends or family camp at your hook-up site with a tent , up to two tents will be allowed per approval from management. They will be charged as follows: | A tent will be charged $42 per night if the tent is added with the RV at the time the RV makes its reservation for the current year or by August 31. | They must pay for at least one night at that time and can add additional", " booked for the current year, the person tenting will be charged full-hook-up rates per night. | | | Tent and Non-Hookup RV Reservations: | Tent site (tents, van camper, and motorcycle camper, and pickup camper) rate is $42 per night | Non-Hookup RV (motorhomes, 5th wheels, travel trailers, pop-up (all sizes) etc.) rate is $58/night (2027). Guests wanting to park tow trailers next to their tents or RV's will be charg", " Non-Hookup RV (motorhomes, 5th wheels, travel trailers, pop-up (all sizes) etc.) rate is $58/night (2027). Guests wanting to park tow trailers next to their tents or RV's will be charged for a tent space for each unit ($42). | Checking-In and Changing Site: | All patrons must check in at the campground office before going to your site, even if you know where you are going. | If you would like to change sites, you ma"], "via": "Sturgis Rally Reservations"}]}
